  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 225 PM EST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nThe extended periods begin Saturday morning with the developing \nsurface low center just off the N FL/GA coast becoming the \ndominant weather feature. This low is expected to continue to \ndevelop through the weekend as it moves NE across the Carolinas \nand Mid-Atlantic states into the beginning of next week. With this\nlow center expected to stay east of the area, the most we will se\nacross north and Central GA will be increased cloud cover and \nsome gusty winds. Some portions of East Central GA may see a \nshower or two Sat afternoon through Sun morning with the lows \ncenter proximity just east of the state. There is also another \nweak frontal boundary that moves east across the area Monday but \nit is very weak with little dynamics or associated moisture. Only \nexpecting increased cloud cover again from this frontal passage. \nAt the same time there is a open wave developing along the Mexican\nGulf coast that moves out across the central Gulf by Mon night. \nIncreased moisture from this wave moves into South and Central GA \nTue morning/afternoon. Right now going with 20% to 40% PoPs for \nshowers Tue and Wed. Not seeing much in the way of instability \nwith this so only going showers for now. \n\nHigh temps Sat through Monday will be mainly in the 60s and 70s \nwith a slight cool down Tue and wed with highs in the 50s and 60s.\nLow temps will do the same thing with lows sat through monday in \nthe 40s and 50s then cooling into the 30s and 40s Tue and Wed.",
